    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f1a081b_1a23fea3",
        "filename": "drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 511,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-01T00:08:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. I thought you are using the file only to obtain block_device but sounds like you are using it for writing as well.",
      "parentUuid": "d75fc300_fa35e938",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 494,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 511,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "91adbfe6b62def07c89fb570a65d7abe498431b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "194f48c5_943193f6",
        "filename": "drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 511,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-01T18:14:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I checked with people more experienced with the block layer and their feedback is:\n\nblkdev_get_by_path() should be used in the zram driver. Using struct file or any file API when accessing a block device is wrong. They should submit bio\u0027s directly to the block device. There are multiple examples in the out-of-tree SCST project. SCST is a collection of kernel drivers that exports local storage via a SCSI-over-network protocol. Source code is available at https://github.com/SCST-project/. See also the scst/src/dev_handlers/scst_vdisk.c file in that project. We also have an open request to upstream the change for ZRAM driver to use blkdev_get_by_path() in  https://b.corp.google.com/issues/195421698 (might not be accessible for partners).",
      "parentUuid": "5f1a081b_1a23fea3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 494,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 511,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "91adbfe6b62def07c89fb570a65d7abe498431b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70b650f4_a29aa545",
        "filename": "drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 511,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275554
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-01T20:43:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-fsdevel/patch/20240123-vfs-bdev-file-v2-12-adbd023e19cc@kernel.org/\n\nzram already went with bdev_file_open_by_dev on upstream, which is also exported symbol",
      "parentUuid": "194f48c5_943193f6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 494,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 511,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "91adbfe6b62def07c89fb570a65d7abe498431b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8450beea_035ff679",
        "filename": "drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 511,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275554
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-01T22:06:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sandeep corrected me that I took a look wrong line. Thanks.\n\nYeah, zram is using filp_open in upstream now and I think zram can change it with blkdev_get_by_path in upstream. But what\u0027s the reason since other drivers in the upstream are already using the filp_open?",
      "parentUuid": "70b650f4_a29aa545",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 494,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 511,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "91adbfe6b62def07c89fb570a65d7abe498431b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "161a86b7_b93d4b63",
        "filename": "drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 511,
      "author": {
        "id": 1954115
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T17:24:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As pointed out by Minchan, not allowing filp_open() in drivers seems like Android\u0027s decision. So we need better reason to replace filp_open() in zram with alternative to push this upstream. Until then, we need to carry this filp_open_block() workaround as `ANDROID:` patch.",
      "parentUuid": "8450beea_035ff679",
      "range": {
